  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>OXO PROCESS (Hydroformylation) is&nbsp;&nbsp;the addition of a hydrogen atom and a formyl group to the molecule of a compound containing a double bond by reaction with hydrogen and carbon monoxide, the chief product being one or more aldehydes.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>Rh</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>catalyst</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>CO</mi></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e8997081-e81d-4f7b-ab65-949e7671610d-image.png\" style=\"width: 308px; height: 167px;\" /></p>",
